  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Haiti&apos;s Response to HIV/AIDS - Haiti (01-Oct-2012-31-Dec-2015)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Haiti has an estimated HIV prevalence among adults of 1.9 percent (UNAIDS Report on the Global AIDS Epidemic 2010). Only 43 percent of the estimated 60,000 people in need of antiretroviral therapy were receiving it in 2009 according to the same report. This grant consolidates two previous Global Fund HIV grants to Haiti (Round 1 Rolling Continuation Channel and Round 5 Phase 2) to provide an integrated approach to HIV services. Services covered by the constituent grants will continue to be funded. Prevention activities include behavior change communication campaigns, promotion of condom use targeting youth, female sex workers and men who have sex with men; voluntary counseling and testing; antiretroviral prophylaxis for pregnant women to prevent mother-to-child transmission of the virus; initiating TB prophylaxis for newly detected seropositive persons; and blood safety precautions. Treatment will focus on providing antiretroviral therapy for people living with advanced HIV infection, and treatment for sexually transmitted infections and opportunistic infections. Care and support activities will focus on community-based interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
